- JSON - Java Script Object Notation
- It is format to store and exchange data i.e. to send to API as a request and also API returns the data base in JSON format as a response.
- The data is stored in the form of key:value pair seperated a comma
- REST APIs will accept and give JSON data, whereas SOAP API will expect XML type of data.

Ex :
{
    "name": "Samarth",
    "age": "25",
    "skills": [
        "python",
        "manual testing",
        "sql"
    ],
    "skills experience": {
        "python": "3",
        "manual testing": "2",
        "sql": "2.5"
    }
}

Note :
- The key & value(str values) should be in "", not in ''
- Each key can i have one value or more than one .i.e. array & also can have JSON object etc..
- In JSON bool values will be true and false in python True and False
- In JSON null but in Python None
- In JSON "" for all str values, in python '' or "" .,
- In JSON 'JSON Object' in python dic
- IN JOSN array in python list

JSON Path
===========
It is the path of a particular key in the JSON data.